# Link Detonator settings. Every line is optional, and the values shown are the defaults
# from app/config.py. On the VM, provision.sh copies this file to
# /etc/link-detonator/app.env, which systemd loads. The app does not read a .env file by
# itself; locally, use `make dev` or export variables in your shell.
#
# Leave a line commented unless you mean to change it. Keep comments on their own line,
# because systemd would read a trailing comment as part of the value. Never put real
# secrets in this example file.

# Sandbox
# LD_IMAGE=link-detonator-worker:latest
# Set to runsc if gVisor is installed on the VM.
# LD_RUNTIME=
# With LD_RUNTIME=runsc, the browser needs a resolver file, because gVisor cannot reach
# Docker's embedded DNS. provision.sh writes this one from the firewall's DNS servers.
# LD_SANDBOX_RESOLV_CONF=/etc/link-detonator/sandbox-resolv.conf
# Keep Chromium's own sandbox on. Works only under gVisor; under runc Chromium cannot start.
# LD_CHROMIUM_SANDBOX=0
# The QR and email decoders' runtime, with no network.
# LD_DECODER_RUNTIME=
# The worker is told to stop at 75% of this, so its final report beats the host's kill.
# LD_DEADLINE_S=60
# Secrets audited against each container, by name. A variable whose name looks like a key,
# token, password or secret is audited as well, and so is a random canary the app plants
# at startup. Add a new key's name here anyway when you add the key.
# LD_SECRET_ENV_NAMES=VULTR_API_KEY,LD_LIVE_ACCESS_CODE

# Scans
# LD_CONCURRENCY=2
# LD_QUEUE_SIZE=10
# LD_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# LD_DISK_CAP_MB=2048
# Defaults to data/ in the project directory.
# LD_DATA_DIR=

# API
# LD_RATE_PER_MINUTE=5
# LD_RATE_PER_HOUR=30
# provision.sh sets this to 1, since Caddy is in front.
# LD_TRUST_PROXY=0

# Reads (snapshots, event streams, screenshots), per client.
# LD_READ_RATE_PER_MINUTE=240
# LD_MAX_STREAMS_PER_CLIENT=4

# Live URL scans run a stranger's JavaScript from this VM's address. They stay off until a
# code is set here, and only people given the code can start one. Use a long random value.
# LD_LIVE_ACCESS_CODE=
# Kill switch: set to 0 and restart to stop live scans. Test charges keep working.
# LD_LIVE_SCANS_ENABLED=1
# LD_LIVE_SCANS_PER_DAY=50

# Budgets across all clients.
# LD_GLOBAL_SCANS_PER_HOUR=120
# LD_MAX_ACTIVE_PER_CLIENT=2
# Queue places only an access-code holder can take, so a full queue cannot lock out a demo.
# LD_RESERVED_QUEUE_SLOTS=2

# Local development only. Never set this on the VM.
# LD_DEV_LOCAL_RUNNER=0
# LD_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Agent. Without VULTR_API_KEY the verdict stays pending; there is no stand-in model.
# Put the real key only in /etc/link-detonator/app.env on the VM, never in this file.
# VULTR_API_KEY=
# LD_LLM_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash
# LD_LLM_CALLS_PER_DAY=400
# LD_AGENT_MAX_FOLLOWUPS=2
# glm-5.3-flash reasons before answering, and reasoning counts against the token cap.
# LD_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# LD_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=4000
